WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:03.080
There are 24 hours in a day but no matter what,

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:06.720
we never feel like it's enough time to get anything done.

3
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.880
A lot of us feel that way.

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.100
We feel pressure to never be late,

5
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:13.370
or when we do, oh God it's like unforgivable

6
00:00:13.370 --> 00:00:14.990
and it's something we struggle with.

7
00:00:14.990 --> 00:00:18.580
So, I wanna break the cycle of bad time management

8
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:20.680
to give us all a feel of control in our day,

9
00:00:20.680 --> 00:00:23.593
but first let's take a look at Helen's story.

10
00:00:23.593 --> 00:00:26.193
(clock ticking)

11
00:00:26.193 --> 00:00:27.480
I just woke up

12
00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:30.990
but somehow I already feel like I'm running late.

13
00:00:30.990 --> 00:00:33.320
I need to get the kids ready for school.

14
00:00:33.320 --> 00:00:35.370
I need to get myself ready for work.

15
00:00:35.370 --> 00:00:39.373
So here goes another fun busy day.

16
00:00:41.060 --> 00:00:46.060
I came upstairs to get my makeup done for work

17
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:52.750
and I realized that my makeup is at my office

18
00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:56.610
because yesterday I had to run out so fast

19
00:00:56.610 --> 00:00:58.260
that I didn't have time to do it.

20
00:00:58.260 --> 00:00:59.820
The kids are all set for school,

21
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:01.760
leave at eight, their lunch is ready,

22
00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.458
and I'm out.

23
00:01:03.458 --> 00:01:05.440
(clock ticking)

24
00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:09.410
I need to like be on another call in about 10 minutes.

25
00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:12.450
Realized that I didn't bring any snacks with me today

26
00:01:12.450 --> 00:01:15.300
but I usually order something to the office

27
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:16.930
and eat at my desk anyhow.

28
00:01:16.930 --> 00:01:21.430
Today I'm lucky because I have my coffee still

29
00:01:21.430 --> 00:01:22.440
from this morning

30
00:01:22.440 --> 00:01:24.510
then that's gonna be my lunch for the day.

31
00:01:24.510 --> 00:01:25.740
(clock ticking)

32
00:01:25.740 --> 00:01:27.390
I thought I would get to come home today

33
00:01:27.390 --> 00:01:30.910
by about five, 5:30, but I was running a little late.

34
00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:33.470
I'm going to start making dinner

35
00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.880
and then I'm gonna spend some time with the kids

36
00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.434
and I will get back to work.

37
00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.300
(clock ticking)

38
00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:45.300
I've been sitting here working for the last hour and a half.

39
00:01:45.520 --> 00:01:46.620
Now I'm looking around

40
00:01:46.620 --> 00:01:49.210
and the whole house is a complete mess.

41
00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:52.700
So I'm gonna go do the dishes and get cleaned up

42
00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:57.090
and then we do it all over again.

43
00:01:57.090 --> 00:02:01.593
It seems like so much got done and nothing got done.

44
00:02:03.352 --> 00:02:06.480
(audience claps)

45
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:09.580
Helen, I can't even look at you.

46
00:02:09.580 --> 00:02:11.660
All right, I'm gonna face you now.

47
00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:14.710
And the reason why is because I cried

48
00:02:14.710 --> 00:02:16.203
when I watched your video.

49
00:02:18.080 --> 00:02:23.080
I so relate to so many things you said.

50
00:02:24.400 --> 00:02:29.350
Do you feel like an overall weight in your life

51
00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:30.853
about time management?

52
00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.760
You know, I run my own law practice

53
00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:38.120
and I have two kids in elementary school

54
00:02:38.120 --> 00:02:41.620
and I'm on the PTA and I'm class mom

55
00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:44.100
and there's always no time.

56
00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:45.540
There's never time.

57
00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:48.260
I mean, it's just an, it's always stressful.

58
00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:51.560
The pressure is on me to get everything done.

59
00:02:51.560 --> 00:02:53.960
And yeah, there's always a weight

60
00:02:53.960 --> 00:02:56.480 line:15%
that hangs over you that, did I get this done?

61
00:02:56.480 --> 00:02:58.180 line:15%
Did I get this for my son?

62
00:02:58.180 --> 00:02:59.750 line:15%
Did I do this for the school?

63
00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:00.870 line:15%
Did I do this for work?

64
00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:02.660 line:15%
There's always that weight.

65
00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:04.360 line:15%
Well, see, when I'm talking to you,

66
00:03:04.360 --> 00:03:06.130
I can see you so objectively.

67
00:03:06.130 --> 00:03:09.500
I'm like, listen, maybe you don't need to be on the PTA.

68
00:03:09.500 --> 00:03:11.460
Maybe you're just a working mom

69
00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.740
and that's already infinite boxes to check.

70
00:03:14.740 --> 00:03:17.560
And maybe there's stuff that can come off the table.

71
00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:21.060
When I say that, how does, what goes on in your head?

72
00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.690
I want to do everything.

73
00:03:22.690 --> 00:03:23.763
Aha! Okay.

74
00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.320
You know, it's almost like I'm a glutton for punishment.

75
00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:32.520
Okay. So how do you break the cycle

76
00:03:32.520 --> 00:03:35.410
of feeling overwhelmed

77
00:03:35.410 --> 00:03:37.280
and daunted by everything you have to do

78
00:03:37.280 --> 00:03:39.293
and start forgiving yourself?

79
00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.400
I don't know.

80
00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:42.880
I just...

81
00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:45.780
The things I do, I wanna do.

82
00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:48.140
I love my job and I love my kids

83
00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:51.080
and I love being there for them and being active.

84
00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.640
So how do I break the cycle?

85
00:03:52.640 --> 00:03:54.550
That's one of my biggest struggles.

86
00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:57.460
'Cause when I watch your video, I do sense a weight.

87
00:03:57.460 --> 00:04:00.820
Like it's not, like, you're not light as a feather about it.

88
00:04:00.820 --> 00:04:04.170
You're like, this is heavy stuff that I'm grappling with.

89
00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:07.590
And if you're piling it all on the plate,

90
00:04:07.590 --> 00:04:11.870
then you either have to take some stuff off the plate

91
00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:16.080
or start feeling fortified about all your choices.

92
00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:19.070
And I wanna tell you, like, lighten up,

93
00:04:19.070 --> 00:04:20.440
like, feel good about it,

94
00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.730
you're being amazing.

95
00:04:22.730 --> 00:04:24.480
Look at all that you're doing.

96
00:04:24.480 --> 00:04:26.250
Like, (finger snap) screw it.

97
00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.030
You should be patting yourself on the back.

98
00:04:29.030 --> 00:04:31.210
Yeah. Some days you do.

99
00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:35.030
And then most days you're just making it through. (laughs)

100
00:04:35.030 --> 00:04:37.263
So how do you break the cycle?

101
00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.330
You know, I don't know.

102
00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:44.690
I feel like maybe it is lightening up the load a little bit,

103
00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:48.220
but I think that the cycle keeps going

104
00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.500
if you want to do all those things.

105
00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:52.050
I wanna do it all too.

106
00:04:52.050 --> 00:04:52.883
I really do.

107
00:04:52.883 --> 00:04:54.180
Like at no point in my life.

108
00:04:54.180 --> 00:04:56.170
I started working when I was in diapers.

109
00:04:56.170 --> 00:05:01.170
So, I hope at some point I am in diapers, still working.

110
00:05:03.187 --> 00:05:04.190
(audience laughs)

111
00:05:04.190 --> 00:05:06.240
Yes, that's right.

112
00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.740
I started there, I plan to end there

113
00:05:09.950 --> 00:05:14.950
and yet I haven't changed certain behaviors in my life

114
00:05:15.260 --> 00:05:18.470
that might lead to better time management.

115
00:05:18.470 --> 00:05:19.890
And when I say lighten up,

116
00:05:19.890 --> 00:05:21.610
I mean if you're gonna make all these choices

117
00:05:21.610 --> 00:05:23.360
then just be lighter about it,

118
00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.490
leave the plate heavy.

119
00:05:25.490 --> 00:05:27.630
Do you think you can do that?

120
00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:29.590
Yeah. I mean, I try to lighten up

121
00:05:29.590 --> 00:05:30.960
but some days you're just,

122
00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:31.840
you just, can't.

123
00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.130
Like at the end of the day, you're like,

124
00:05:34.130 --> 00:05:35.500
I need to do this, I need to do that.

125
00:05:35.500 --> 00:05:36.333
What did I accomplish?

126
00:05:36.333 --> 00:05:39.550
You feel pulled down by all the choices you made

127
00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:41.250
and boxes you have to check.

128
00:05:41.250 --> 00:05:42.200
Right.

129
00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.920
So, do you think your time management issue

130
00:05:45.920 --> 00:05:47.710
is more about making peace

131
00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:49.290
with all that you've put on your plate

132
00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:52.293
rather than being on time to every appointment?

133
00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:54.380
Yeah, possibly.

134
00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:55.670
I'm hard on myself.

135
00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:57.660
I feel like I look back and I say

136
00:05:57.660 --> 00:05:59.140
I wanna be the best at my job.

137
00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:00.390
I wanna be the best mom.

138
00:06:00.390 --> 00:06:02.370
I wanna be the best wife.

139
00:06:02.370 --> 00:06:04.440
I mean, you know, like you wanna be the best

140
00:06:04.440 --> 00:06:05.470
in everything you do

141
00:06:05.470 --> 00:06:08.050
and it's hard to be the best in everything.

142
00:06:08.050 --> 00:06:09.950
Something takes a toll eventually.

143
00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:13.530
Where does best measure up to you?

144
00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:15.603
Where does the source of what's best?

145
00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:21.790
I just, I guess it's probably just the way I was raised.

146
00:06:21.790 --> 00:06:23.600
I think that my parents,

147
00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:24.670
I'm first generation American

148
00:06:24.670 --> 00:06:25.890
my parents came from Russia

149
00:06:25.890 --> 00:06:28.710
and they had to work, work, work, work, work,

150
00:06:28.710 --> 00:06:31.920
you know, to always do their best.

151
00:06:31.920 --> 00:06:35.180
And the best was always expected of me, you know?

152
00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:37.070
'Cause they didn't come here for nothing

153
00:06:37.070 --> 00:06:38.110
as my dad would say. (laughs)

154
00:06:38.110 --> 00:06:40.530
So I always had to do, do, do.

155
00:06:40.530 --> 00:06:43.670
And I guess that transfers over into now.

156
00:06:43.670 --> 00:06:47.250
Trying to be the best in everything, so.

157
00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.560
I see a pattern.

158
00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.030 line:15%
Like I see a burning fire

159
00:06:51.030 --> 00:06:54.560 line:15%
and mine is because my parents were the exact opposite.

160
00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:58.140
Like they, you know, they were so Bohemian

161
00:06:58.140 --> 00:07:00.770
that it turned me into the other direction.

162
00:07:00.770 --> 00:07:04.090
Like it lit some type of fire of accountability

163
00:07:04.090 --> 00:07:05.370
and work as my parent

164
00:07:05.370 --> 00:07:07.963
and something that was incredibly structured.

165
00:07:09.049 --> 00:07:10.770
I definitely need to know

166
00:07:10.770 --> 00:07:14.870
how to not be five minutes late every time

167
00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.270
but I wanna be five minutes early

168
00:07:17.270 --> 00:07:19.170
and like be able to waste time

169
00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:21.083
and luxury in time.

170
00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.337
I totally feel you.

171
00:07:23.337 --> 00:07:25.670
The struggle is real. (laughs)

172
00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.160
With the time, with the clock

173
00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.430
I'm always, what time is it?

174
00:07:28.430 --> 00:07:29.263
What time is it?

175
00:07:29.263 --> 00:07:30.940
My six year old gets annoyed with me.

176
00:07:30.940 --> 00:07:33.810
I feel like I'm not usually happy with the result too.

177
00:07:33.810 --> 00:07:36.639
Like it's, usually my reaction to time is like,

178
00:07:36.639 --> 00:07:38.723
(screams) it's what?

179
00:07:38.723 --> 00:07:42.018
It's never like, oh cool, it's that?

180
00:07:42.018 --> 00:07:43.540
Whew! Got ya.

181
00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:46.760
I'm literally like, I'm screwing up again.

182
00:07:46.760 --> 00:07:48.098
Is what time it is.

183
00:07:48.098 --> 00:07:50.681
(upbeat music)

